Invocation: `/impeccable <command>` in Claude and Codex, or `$impeccable <command>` in Codex.

## Environments

- **WSL** (Pawnther, Codex CLI, Claude Code): everything above. `PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_BROWSER=chromium` is exported in 
`~/.profile` and `~/.bashrc`. Impeccable hooks: `~/.codex/hooks.json` (approve once in Codex under `/hooks`) and 
`~/.claude/settings.local.json`.
- **Windows-native Codex app / Claude desktop app**: knowledge skills; use the app's built-in browser for screenshots. 
Windows has no Node on PATH, so Impeccable hooks and Playwright CLI stay in WSL. The Claude desktop app runs the 
Chrome DevTools MCP through `wsl.exe` (user config in `C:\Users\momoy\.claude.json`).
- When the Codex app runs its agent in WSL mode, its built-in browser is unavailable; the WSL tools cover that.

